  "measurementLimits": [
    "One unmodified Ethereum replay, not an optimized variant or a multichain benchmark.",
    "Envio metrics are an interim scrape. The CLI exited before the final scrape; counters are lower bounds, not final totals.",
    "Effect waits and handler times can overlap and nest. Do not sum them as a wall-time decomposition or promised savings.",
    "Fetch instrumentation measures until response headers, not full body consumption; envelope concurrency is not logical RPC concurrency.",
    "Native Envio already preloads checkpoints concurrently. Low envelope concurrency does not prove single-RPC operation.",
    "CPU time includes process/native threads and is not an independent additive wall-time share.",
    "Upstream RPS is an average; fixed-window bursts, Alchemy CU weights, other apps and proxy replicas remain constraints.",
    "No proposed change has been implemented or benchmarked. Expected gain remains a hypothesis."
  ],
  "proposal": [
    "Coordinate finite getter/raw-call/code-verification effect budgets; test 35 then 40 versus current 25, retaining 8-active/256-waiter RPC guard and aggregate eRPC cap 50. Add bounded read prefetch only where metrics show underfilled independent work; apply entity updates in original order.",
    "Group canonical checks into bounded observation phases with fresh opening/final acceptance checks for every unique anchor, complete block-hash pins, staged state updates and rejection on any changed anchor.",
    "Defer per-chain workers until a separate 19-entity partitioning/migration and multi-chain replay/reorg plan is approved.",
    "Defer selective Multicall3 until caller independence, exact historical block pins, deployment boundaries and per-item revert semantics are proven.",
    "Treat moving source-proof discovery out of the getter path as cold-start resilience work, not the primary 50-100% speed lever."
  ],
